<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43904" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐήκο-ος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐυάκος</span></b> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκοή</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hearing well</i> or
			<i>easily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				3.17
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hearing willingly, obedient</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1102b27
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>inclined to give ear</i>, of the gods, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θνατοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.316.5
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).101
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				105
			</span></i> (Mytil.); written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐήκουος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				4607.5
			</span></i>: generally, <i>inclined</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς μεταβολήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					2.14.5
				</span></i>
			 (
				Sup.
			). Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, διακεῖσθαι πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					27.7.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>easily heard, audible</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Top.</u>
				107b2
			</span></i>; -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οώτερα τὰ τῆς νυκτός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					899a19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>pleasant to the ear, agreeable</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
				εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				48
			</span></i>, al.</div>
